            <p>Many popular cruise lines that travel through the Caribbean make a stop in Cozumel. Regular stops in Cozumel are made by <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/royal-caribbean-cruises.aspx">Royal Caribbean</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/carnival-cruise-line.aspx">Carnival Cruise Lines</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/norwegian-cruise-line.aspx">Norwegian Cruise Line</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/msc-cruise-line.aspx">MSC Cruises</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/disney-cruise-line.aspx"> Disney Cruise Line </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/princess-cruises.aspx"> Princess Cruises </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/celebrity-cruise-line.aspx"> Celebrity Cruises </a>, and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/holland-america-cruises.aspx"> Holland America Line </a>. These cruise lines transport thousands of tourists to the island annually, making it one of the most trafficked and crowded cruise destinations in the Caribbean. </p>

            <p>Each cruise line has a slightly different onboard experience leading up to Cozumel. Royal Caribbean brings to mind large ships with entertainment, innovation, and fun; Carnival Cruise Line conjures up a party at sea with its lively, social vibe. Norwegian Cruise Line focuses on flexibility, and MSC Cruises mingles European style with Caribbean warmth. This variety accommodates the traveler looking for a cruise to Cozumel according to personal preference and expectation. </p>

